From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hao Li <hao.x.li@intel.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:37:33 -0700
Subject: Fix use-after-free for empty buffer/texture copy workarounds

Empty buffer-texture copies (zero-sized copy extents) skipped command
recording within certain workaround paths (e.g., blit-to-depth/stencil,
oversized-row split). Because mTopLevelBuffers and mTopLevelTextures
held raw pointers, and the only Ref keeping them alive was the recorded
command, skipping recording left these pointers dangling, causing a UAF
in QueueBase::ValidateSubmit.

Add an early-out for empty copies in APICopyBufferToTexture,
APICopyTextureToBuffer, and APICopyTextureToTexture. They now record the
plain copy command and return before any workaround runs.
- Add DAWN_CHECK(!copyExtent.IsEmpty()) to workarounds as a release-mode
  backstop.
- Add regression tests for empty B2T and T2B copies.

Bug: 571648522
Change-Id: I88bd7f82df6a27a39c65747eb49a768e4f00f13f
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/350415
